12. Exact Repeat and No-Spin

Two evaluations over identical validated source and revise material produce an
equal TransitionDecisionV01 with equal canonical bytes. Independent queue
advances produce equal DEADEND entries and artifacts with equal canonical
bytes and stable IDs. Both retain the unchanged budget log. Reentry from the
terminal DEADEND entry fails with g2d_terminal_queue_reentry_forbidden.

No cache, mutable global, wall-clock branch, random ID, UUID, or call-order
dependency was added. The path is deterministic, bounded, non-mutating, and
cannot consume additional budget or create an unbounded revise loop from
identical evidence.

13. Complete Negative Matrix and Anti-Gaming

Executable public-path tests reject:
- a manually forged revise observation ID;
- eligible revise substituted for terminal no-progress;
- changed repeated progress/evidence material;
- wrong derived terminal state;
- wrong revise reason;
- wrong revision index and invalid final revision index;
- wrong cell ID and queue-entry ID;
- wrong cell-budget and global-budget objects or IDs;
- wrong historical t06 origin;
- missing settled revise observation;
- foreign or stale validation report;
- changed source outputs, evidence, advisories, or queue reasons;
- a non-D3-local node;
- revise-reason contamination of target queue reasons;
- an attempted t12 budget successor.

The strengthened test contains 65 assertions and 11 executable raises checks,
compared with 7 and 1 in the accepted parent. It reaches the real public revise,
transition, and queue-advance functions. No callable-only, hasattr-only,
source-name-only, empty-tuple uniqueness, manual PASS, skip, xfail, or private
helper substitute serves as behavioral evidence.

